  "mnFatha": "A short “a”. A small stroke above the letter — one count, like one clap.",
  "mnKasra": "A short “i”. A small stroke below the letter — one count.",
  "mnDamma": "A short “u”. A tiny wāw above the letter — one count.",
  "mnSukun": "No vowel: the letter is sākin. Join it to the vowel before it.",
  "mnShadda": "Doubling: the letter is pronounced twice — first with sukūn, then with a vowel.",
  "mnFathatan": "Tanwīn of fatḥ: an extra “n” sound. Two strokes above.",
  "mnKasratan": "Tanwīn of kasr: “-in”. Two strokes below.",
  "mnDammatan": "Tanwīn of ḍamm: “-un”. Two tiny wāws above.",
  "mnMadd2": "Natural lengthening with ا / و / ي — exactly TWO counts. Never rush it.",
  "mnLin": "Soft wāw or yā’ with sukūn after a fatḥah — a gentle glide.",
  "mnMaddah": "Hamzah followed by alif written as one sign — read with madd.",
  "mnMadd4": "Madd letter meets hamzah in the SAME word — stretch FOUR (to five) counts. Obligatory.",
  "mnMadd45": "Madd at the end of a word, hamzah starts the NEXT word — four (to five) counts.",
  "mnMadd6": "Madd followed by a permanent sukūn or shaddah — SIX full counts, the longest.",
  "mnMadd246": "Stopping turns the last vowel into sukūn after a madd letter — 2, 4 or 6 counts.",
  "mnWasl": "Pronounced when you START with it, silent when you join from the previous word.",
  "tjGhunnahTrig": "Nūn or mīm with shaddah (نّ / مّ).",
  "tjGhunnahHow": "A full nasal hum from the nose, held two counts.",
  "tjIzharTrig": "Nūn sākinah or tanwīn before a throat letter (ء ه ع ح غ خ).",
  "tjIzharHow": "Pronounce the nūn clearly and quickly — no nasalization, no pause.",
  "tjIdghamGTrig": "Nūn sākinah / tanwīn before ي ن م و (across two words).",
  "tjIdghamGHow": "Merge the nūn into the next letter while humming two counts.",
  "tjIdghamNgTrig": "Nūn sākinah / tanwīn before ل or ر.",
  "tjIdghamNgHow": "Merge completely into the lām or rā’ — the nūn disappears.",
  "tjIqlabTrig": "Nūn sākinah / tanwīn before ب.",
  "tjIqlabHow": "Flip the nūn into a light mīm, hidden with ghunnah, two counts.",
  "tjIkhfaTrig": "Nūn sākinah / tanwīn before the remaining 15 letters.",
  "tjIkhfaHow": "Hide the nūn between iẓhār and idghām — a soft hum shaped toward the next letter.",
  "tjQalqalahTrig": "ق ط ب ج د with sukūn — or at a stop. Remember: قُطْبُ جَدٍّ.",
  "tjQalqalahHow": "An echoing bounce: release the letter with a small pop, strongest when stopping.",
  "tjIkhfaShafawiTrig": "Mīm sākinah before ب.",
  "tjIkhfaShafawiHow": "Hide the mīm at the lips with ghunnah.",
  "tjIdghamShafawiTrig": "Mīm sākinah before another mīm.",
  "tjIdghamShafawiHow": "Merge the two mīms with a full ghunnah.",
  "tjMadd2Trig": "A plain madd letter (ا و ي) with nothing after it.",
  "tjMadd2How": "Exactly two counts.",
  "tjMadd4Trig": "Madd letter + hamzah in the same word.",
  "tjMadd4How": "Four to five counts — obligatory.",
  "tjMadd45Trig": "Madd at a word end, hamzah begins the next word.",
  "tjMadd45How": "Four to five counts in Ḥafṣ (other transmissions differ — see Qirā’āt).",
  "tjMadd6Trig": "Madd letter followed by a permanent sukūn or shaddah.",
  "tjMadd6How": "Six full counts — including the opening letters like الٓمٓ.",
  "tjShamsiyyaTrig": "“ال” before a sun letter — the lām is written but silent.",
  "tjShamsiyyaHow": "Jump straight to the doubled sun letter.",
  "tjQamariyyaTrig": "“ال” before a moon letter — the lām is pronounced with sukūn.",
  "tjQamariyyaHow": "Say the lām clearly: al-qamar.",
  "tjTafkhimTrig": "The seven heavy letters: خ ص ض غ ط ق ظ.",
  "tjTafkhimHow": "Fill the mouth with the sound — these letters are heavy at every vowel.",
  "tjIzharShafawiTrig": "Mīm sākinah before any letter except م or ب.",
  "tjIzharShafawiHow": "Pronounce the mīm clearly with closed lips — no hiding, no merging.",
  "tjRaaTafkhimTrig": "Rā’ with fatḥah or ḍammah, or sākinah after one.",
  "tjRaaTafkhimHow": "A heavy, full-mouthed rā’ — round the back of the tongue.",
  "tjRaaTarqiqTrig": "Rā’ with kasrah, or sākinah after one.",
  "tjRaaTarqiqHow": "A light, thin rā’ — no rounding, no heaviness.",
  "tjLamJalalahTrig": "The lām of ٱللَّٰه — Allāh’s name.",
  "tjLamJalalahHow": "Heavy after fatḥah/ḍammah, light after kasrah.",
